course: dictionary
lesson: 10005
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word telling can change its meaning depending on the words around it. Context, the words and sentences around a word, is your best clue. In «She is telling a story», telling means saying or reporting something. Here it is a form of the verb tell.
explain: Telling can also be an adjective, a describing word. «A telling remark» is a remark that shows something important, often more than the speaker meant to show. «A telling blow» is a blow with a strong effect. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and asking whether it still makes sense.
explain: Telling can be a noun too, meaning the act of telling a story: «In this telling of the tale, the wolf is kind.» Some phrases change the meaning again. «Telling off» means a scolding, and «there's no telling» means there is no way to know.
fact: Telling is a form of the verb tell: tell, tells, told, telling.
fact: «A telling detail» shows a character's feelings or gives a clue.
fact: «A telling sign» is a sign that shows something clearly.
fact: «I got a telling-off for being late» means I was scolded for being late.
fact: «Stories also grow in the telling»: a story can change each time it is passed on.
exercise: «She is telling a story about a dragon.» In this sentence, telling means | Scolding someone | Showing something important | Having a strong effect | *Saying or reporting something
exercise: «The muddy boots were a telling detail.» What does telling mean here? | A story told long ago | Being very loud | *Showing something important | Scolding someone
exercise: Which phrase means a scolding? | there's no telling | a telling blow | a telling sign | *telling off
test: «In this telling of the tale, the wolf is kind.» In this sentence, telling is a | Adjective | Verb | Phrase | *Noun
test: «There's no telling what will happen next.» What does this phrase mean? | A scolding is coming | *There is no way to know | Someone is telling a secret | It will definitely happen
exam: Jayden says, «Her silence was telling.» What does telling mean here? | *Showing something important, more than she meant to show | A scolding from a teacher | Saying something out loud | Counting the time on a clock
